==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Wall Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Eraser Cat''' when obtained from [[Demon Eraser (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], Brainwashed Tank Cat is a short-ranged, disposable unit meant to take the hits in place of others, protecting damage dealers from enemies, but it doesn't quite work the same way. Unlike Tank Cat, its recharge time, regardless of [[Relativity Clock]] [[Treasure]]s, can never reach the minimum and its health easily falls behind too, though it will still be more than Tank Cat's early in the game.

Since Brainwashed Wall Cat ends up with about half the health and twice the recharge of Eraser and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank/Manic Eraser]] as the game progresses, the protection it gives turns out to only be a little more than '''a fourth''' of that provided by the other two. Luckily, its resistance does make it '''four times''' as tough against Traitless, not only making up for the stats, but allowing for improvement through combos that the other Erasers have no access to. It doesn't have much of a breakaway stat-wise, so it should still only be considered for use in stages where all damage of relevance comes from Traitless enemies, as it ends up severely outclassed otherwise.

Due to the way it works (more health, less recharge, assuming the opponents are Traitless), Brainwashed Wall Cat is more susceptible to overkill damage, thus less recommended against armies with high DPS, where even [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Basic]] [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cat]] [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|variants]] may be more effective, but Brainwashed Wall Cat does tend to work better against enemies with high damage per hit, such as [[THE SLOTH]].

It is a secondary meatshield, just like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu Cat]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], etc. and can be used with the [[Cat Combo|Combos]] [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] and [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] to make up for their poor recharge time.

==='''True Form'''===
Brainwashed Eraser Cat gains 4 more speed and the Insanely Tough ability, replacing the Resistant ability. While the defense boost against Traitless is quite large, it still keeps all the flaws of its previous forms. However, using it with [[Haniwa Cat|Haniwa]] allows for some decent anti-Traitless stall; if you have a Research Power Up combo like [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]] or [[Sigh of Relief (Combo)|Sigh of Relief]], Brainwashed Eraser's effectiveness rises and makes it a decent cat.

Overall, it's still a fairly situational unit, but now performs even better in those rare scenarios where you need to use it.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

